Some strategies that can be used to entice people with the promise of economic rewards in order to trap them into forced labor include: 
1. Fraudulently representing the labor as volunteer work or an internship; 
2. Offering exploitative working conditions with few rights or protections; 
3. Misrepresenting the wages/salary that will be earned; and/or
4. Taking deposits or charging fees from job seekers under false pretenses.

In addition, people should be aware of recruitment scams which may offer high salary jobs that require applicants to pay for certifications, provide personal information, submit employment applications/taxes/fees and sign contracts obligating them to work at a certain wage. Furthermore, once someone is working under these conditions it’s important for them to know their rights so they can attempt to extricate themselves from the situation safely.
